		{"id":"02442c88fc012fd1","x":-500,"y":-360,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"[[Player Characters.base]]\n#PlayerCharacter "},
		{"id":"f36cd5d877bc4e2a","x":-500,"y":-240,"width":1925,"height":550,"type":"text","text":"\n\nGimmick \tConflict \tWant \nStoic Cold Captain. No loose ends kind of person, but loyal.\tSurvivor's Guilt.  Fish out of Temporal Water\tFind or resolve whatever caused her expedition to die. Find a new place in this new world\nBorn in Vasselhiem, Lucy was raised among sailors, traders, and the salt of the sea. Her people were known for their strength and endurance, and from a young age she was drawn to the rhythm of the tides and the call of the deep. She joined a merchant or exploration fleet in her youth, quickly rising through the ranks thanks to her discipline, calm command, and knack for reading weather and people alike.\nShe earned respect not through charisma, but through competence, the kind of leader whose crew followed her because she never asked what she wouldn’t do herself. Her reputation grew as a steadfast captain who could guide a ship through storms that would break lesser souls.\nWhen she accepted a commission to explore the northern polar seas, it was meant to be her crowning achievement — to chart routes where no ship had sailed, to uncover rumors of lost druidic relics beneath the ice. But the journey turned dire as the sky darkened and the ocean itself rebelled.\nAn unnatural something descended, a storm, a monster maybe? . She fought to save her ship until the last moment, even losing her arm. After the something happened, her ship was torn down and everyone perished.\nWhen she awoke, she had been entombed in ice, preserved for decades — maybe centuries. The Druid Circle Name Here, a reclusive group of northern druids (The very hidden druids she set out to find), found her body while tending to the shifting glaciers. Her survival defied reason, the ice had not consumed her, it had kept her. They thawed her carefully, nursing her back to life. The druids claimed the land itself had chosen her\nShe learned their ways, mastering polar magic, but her mind was always half adrift, haunted by the modern world she didn’t recognize and the old one that no longer existed.\nNow after thanking the druids for their help, she travels back to the capital to uncover the history of the current world and the secrets of whatever it was that killed her crew. Struggling with survivors' guilt from her failure as a captain. Too stubborn to just drop down and die, she looks for a new purpose in life and to find out if she can ever lead again.\nFlaws\nNatural Misalignment. (Polar)\nYour connection to nature is local and polar — ice, stone, wind. You cannot switch between Circle of the Land types of land.\nAdditionally. You have disadvantage on Wisdom (Survival), Wisdom (Animal Handling), and Intelligence (Nature) checks in deserts, jungles, or volcanic terrain.\nCaptain’s Burden\nWhenever an ally that you can see is reduced to 0 hit points, or fails a death saving throw, you must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw (DC 15).\nOn a failure, you are immediately compelled to heal them, if it's not possible to heal them in the same turn. You move toward them and take the Dodge or Help action on your turn, if possible.\n"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}